---
title: Mynth
id: mynth-adapter
description: "Generate images with Mynth models like Flux, Recraft, Gemini, Qwen, Seedream, Wan, and Grok Imagine in TanStack AI via the Mynth community adapter."
keywords:
  - tanstack ai
  - mynth
  - image generation
  - flux
  - recraft
  - qwen
  - seedream
  - community adapter
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Mynth adapter gives you access to Mynth image generation models through TanStack AI. It is a community adapter for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateImage()"},{"type":"text","value":" with typed model IDs, normalized image results, image-to-image support, and Mynth-specific request options through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mynth is image-only in this package. Reach for it when you want TanStack AI's image generation workflow with Mynth models such as Flux, Recraft, Gemini, Qwen, Seedream, Wan, and Grok Imagine."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quick note: Mynth is in public beta, so the model lineup and a few request options are still settling. The adapter tracks the Mynth SDK closely, and we welcome feedback on the API and integration experience."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\",\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\",\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\",\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\",\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\",\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\",\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\",\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\",\"@tanstack/ai\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter targets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai"},{"type":"text","value":" 0.34 and newer."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"authentication","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Authentication"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set your Mynth API key in the environment:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"MYNTH_API_KEY=mak_...","lang":"sh"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MYNTH_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" on the server only. Never expose it in browser code or public client environment variables, or it may end up in a client bundle."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can also pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"apiKey"},{"type":"text","value":" directly in the adapter config. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"baseUrl"},{"type":"text","value":" is optional and useful for proxies, tests, or custom deployments."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you need a key, create one in the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://mynth.io/dashboard/keys","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mynth API keys dashboard"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"quick-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quick Start"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { mynthImage } from \"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: mynthImage(\"black-forest-labs/flux.2-dev\"),\n  prompt: \"Editorial product photo of a ceramic mug on a linen tablecloth\",\n  numberOfImages: 1,\n  size: \"square\",\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.id);\nconsole.log(result.model);\nconsole.log(result.images[0]?.url);","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack AI adapters are model-bound, so you choose the Mynth model when you create the adapter."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"reusable-provider","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reusable Provider"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createMynthImage()"},{"type":"text","value":" when you want to share config across multiple adapters:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { createMynthImage } from \"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\";\n\nconst mynth = createMynthImage({\n  apiKey: process.env.MYNTH_API_KEY!,\n  baseUrl: \"https://api.mynth.io\",\n});\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: mynth(\"google/gemini-3.1-flash-image\"),\n  prompt: \"A playful paper-cut illustration of a city park in spring\",\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.images[0]?.url);","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can still override shared config per adapter:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createMynthImage } from \"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\";\n\nconst mynth = createMynthImage();\n\nconst adapter = mynth(\"auto\", {\n  baseUrl: \"https://proxy.example.com\",\n});","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"model-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use TanStack's top-level fields for common options such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prompt"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"numberOfImages"},{"type":"text","value":", and shorthand "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"size"},{"type":"text","value":". Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" for Mynth-specific options:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { mynthImage } from \"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: mynthImage(\"recraft/recraft-v4\"),\n  prompt: \"Modern poster design for a jazz festival\",\n  numberOfImages: 2,\n  size: \"portrait\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    negativePrompt: \"watermark, blurry text\",\n    magicPrompt: true,\n    size: {\n      type: \"aspect_ratio\",\n      aspectRatio: \"4:5\",\n      scale: \"4k\",\n    },\n    output: {\n      format: \"png\",\n      quality: 90,\n    },\n    rating: true,\n    metadata: {\n      requestId: \"req_123\",\n    },\n  },\n});","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Notes:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.negativePrompt"},{"type":"text","value":" maps to Mynth's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"negative_prompt"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.magicPrompt"},{"type":"text","value":" maps to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"magic_prompt"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.rating"},{"type":"text","value":" configures content rating on the result. The older "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"contentRating"},{"type":"text","value":" name still works as an alias"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.promptStructured"},{"type":"text","value":" is still supported for compatibility and expands into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prompt"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"negative_prompt"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"magic_prompt"},{"type":"text","value":". When set, its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"positive"},{"type":"text","value":" overrides the plain "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prompt"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.size"},{"type":"text","value":" overrides the top-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"size"},{"type":"text","value":". Use it when you need structured Mynth size objects, including aspect ratios and an optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scale: \"4k\""}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Top-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"size"},{"type":"text","value":" is for shorthand values such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"auto\""},{"type":"text","value":" and preset strings like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"square\""},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"landscape\""}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.destination"},{"type":"text","value":" delivers the generation to a configured Mynth destination, overriding any adapter-level or env default"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"image-inputs-image-to-image","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Image Inputs (image-to-image)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Models that accept image inputs work with TanStack AI's content-part prompts, so you can mix instruction text with reference images for image-to-image, reference-guided, edit, and try-on flows. The adapter maps the image parts onto Mynth's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inputs"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { mynthImage } from \"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: mynthImage(\"black-forest-labs/flux.2-dev\"),\n  prompt: [\n    { type: \"text\", content: \"Restyle this scene as a watercolor painting\" },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/photo.jpg\" },\n    },\n  ],\n});","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A few things worth knowing:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Only models in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MYNTH_IMAGE_INPUT_MODELS"},{"type":"text","value":" accept image parts. Passing image parts to a text-only model is a compile-time error"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both URL sources ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ type: \"url\", value }"},{"type":"text","value":") and inline data sources ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ type: \"data\", value, mimeType }"},{"type":"text","value":", encoded as a data URI) are supported"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A part's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.role"},{"type":"text","value":" maps to Mynth's input intent. TanStack's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"character\""},{"type":"text","value":" maps directly, and the other generic roles fall back to Mynth's automatic detection"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For Mynth's finer-grained intents ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"person"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"garment"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pose"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"style"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"background"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"product"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"object"},{"type":"text","value":"), pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.inputs"},{"type":"text","value":" with an explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"as"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Image parts from the prompt and entries in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.inputs"},{"type":"text","value":" are combined, with prompt parts first"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"available-models","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available Models"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter exports a runtime list and a type union for supported image models:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { MYNTH_IMAGE_MODELS, type MynthImageModel } from \"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\";\n\nconst defaultModel: MynthImageModel = \"auto\";\n\nfor (const model of MYNTH_IMAGE_MODELS) {\n  console.log(model);\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is handy for model selectors, validation, and keeping client and server code in sync. There is a matching "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MYNTH_IMAGE_INPUT_MODELS"},{"type":"text","value":" list (and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MynthImageInputModel"},{"type":"text","value":" type) for the subset that accepts image inputs."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mynth supports model IDs across multiple providers, including "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"auto"},{"type":"text","value":", Flux, Recraft, Gemini, Qwen, Seedream, Imagine, Wan, Grok Imagine, and try-on models. The exported list is a fixed snapshot for type safety. For the live catalog with pricing, use the models endpoint below."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"models-endpoint","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Models endpoint"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mynth exposes a public catalog at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"https://api.mynth.io/models"},{"type":"text","value":". It does not require an API key, and it carries pricing today with room for more metadata over time. This is the source of truth if you want to render a picker with live pricing rather than the static exported list."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const response = await fetch(\"https://api.mynth.io/models\");\nconst { data } = await response.json();\n\nfor (const model of data) {\n  console.log(model.id, model.displayName, model.pricing);\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each entry looks roughly like this:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"{\n  \"id\": \"black-forest-labs/flux.2-dev\",\n  \"displayName\": \"FLUX.2 Dev\",\n  \"pricing\": {\n    \"perImage\": { \"base\": \"0.01\", \"4k\": \"0.04\" },\n    \"perInput\": \"0.002\",\n  },\n}","lang":"jsonc"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you already use the Mynth SDK, the same data is available through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"new Mynth().models.list()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"streaming-example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Streaming Example"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This adapter also works with TanStack AI's streaming image workflow:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateImage, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { mynthImage } from \"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { prompt, model } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = generateImage({\n    adapter: mynthImage(model ?? \"auto\"),\n    prompt,\n    numberOfImages: 1,\n    stream: true,\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a full example using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useGenerateImage()"},{"type":"text","value":", see the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/mynthio/oss/tree/main/examples/tanstack-start-ai-mynth-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Start + Mynth adapter demo"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"supported-capabilities","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supported Capabilities"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Image generation with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateImage()"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Image-to-image with content-part prompts on input-capable models"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Streaming image generation with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stream: true"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Typed model IDs through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MYNTH_IMAGE_MODELS"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MynthImageModel"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mynth-specific request options through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter returns TanStack AI's normalized image result shape:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":": the Mynth task id"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"model"},{"type":"text","value":": the resolved model returned by Mynth, or the requested model as a fallback"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"images"},{"type":"text","value":": only successful images are included"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"images[*].revisedPrompt"},{"type":"text","value":": included when Mynth enhances the prompt"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"api-reference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API Reference"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"mynthimage-model-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mynthImage(model, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a Mynth image adapter directly."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"model"},{"type":"text","value":": a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MynthImageModel"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"config.apiKey?"},{"type":"text","value":": optional override for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MYNTH_API_KEY"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"config.baseUrl?"},{"type":"text","value":": optional base URL override"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"config.destination?"},{"type":"text","value":": optional default destination for generated images"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MynthImageAdapter"},{"type":"text","value":" for use with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateImage()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createmynthimage-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createMynthImage(config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a reusable provider factory that returns model-bound adapters."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"mynth-image-models","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MYNTH_IMAGE_MODELS"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Readonly array of supported Mynth image model IDs."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"mynthimagemodel","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MynthImageModel"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type union of supported Mynth image model IDs."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"mynth-image-input-models","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MYNTH_IMAGE_INPUT_MODELS"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Readonly array of model IDs that accept image inputs (image-to-image, try-on)."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"mynthimageinputmodel","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MynthImageInputModel"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type union of the model IDs that accept image inputs."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"limitations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Limitations"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This package only provides an image adapter for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateImage()"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It does not provide chat or text-generation adapters"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next Steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/mynthio/oss/tree/main/packages/sdk","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mynth SDK README"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/mynthio/oss/tree/main/examples/tanstack-start-ai-mynth-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Start + Mynth adapter demo"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://mynth.io","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mynth"}]}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"authentication","text":"Authentication","level":2},{"id":"quick-start","text":"Quick Start","level":2},{"id":"reusable-provider","text":"Reusable Provider","level":2},{"id":"model-options","text":"Model Options","level":2},{"id":"image-inputs-image-to-image","text":"Image Inputs (image-to-image)","level":2},{"id":"available-models","text":"Available Models","level":2},{"id":"models-endpoint","text":"Models endpoint","level":3},{"id":"streaming-example","text":"Streaming Example","level":2},{"id":"supported-capabilities","text":"Supported Capabilities","level":2},{"id":"api-reference","text":"API Reference","level":2},{"id":"mynthimage-model-config","text":"mynthImage(model, config?)","level":3},{"id":"createmynthimage-config","text":"createMynthImage(config?)","level":3},{"id":"mynth-image-models","text":"MYNTH_IMAGE_MODELS","level":3},{"id":"mynthimagemodel","text":"MynthImageModel","level":3},{"id":"mynth-image-input-models","text":"MYNTH_IMAGE_INPUT_MODELS","level":3},{"id":"mynthimageinputmodel","text":"MynthImageInputModel","level":3},{"id":"limitations","text":"Limitations","level":2},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next Steps","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe Mynth adapter gives you access to Mynth image generation models through TanStack AI. It is a community adapter for `generateImage()` with typed model IDs, normalized image results, image-to-image support, and Mynth-specific request options through `modelOptions`.\n\nMynth is image-only in this package. Reach for it when you want TanStack AI's image generation workflow with Mynth models such as Flux, Recraft, Gemini, Qwen, Seedream, Wan, and Grok Imagine.\n\nQuick note: Mynth is in public beta, so the model lineup and a few request options are still settling. The adapter tracks the Mynth SDK closely, and we welcome feedback on the API and integration experience.\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter @tanstack/ai\nvue: @mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter @tanstack/ai\nsolid: @mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter @tanstack/ai\nsvelte: @mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter @tanstack/ai\npreact: @mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter @tanstack/ai\nangular: @mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter @tanstack/ai\nvanilla: @mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter @tanstack/ai\noctane: @mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter @tanstack/ai\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nThe adapter targets `@tanstack/ai` 0.34 and newer.\n\n## Authentication\n\nSet your Mynth API key in the environment:\n\n```sh\nMYNTH_API_KEY=mak_...\n```\n\nKeep `MYNTH_API_KEY` on the server only. Never expose it in browser code or public client environment variables, or it may end up in a client bundle.\n\nYou can also pass `apiKey` directly in the adapter config. `baseUrl` is optional and useful for proxies, tests, or custom deployments.\n\nIf you need a key, create one in the [Mynth API keys dashboard](https://mynth.io/dashboard/keys).\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```ts\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { mynthImage } from \"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: mynthImage(\"black-forest-labs/flux.2-dev\"),\n  prompt: \"Editorial product photo of a ceramic mug on a linen tablecloth\",\n  numberOfImages: 1,\n  size: \"square\",\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.id);\nconsole.log(result.model);\nconsole.log(result.images[0]?.url);\n```\n\nTanStack AI adapters are model-bound, so you choose the Mynth model when you create the adapter.\n\n## Reusable Provider\n\nUse `createMynthImage()` when you want to share config across multiple adapters:\n\n```ts\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { createMynthImage } from \"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\";\n\nconst mynth = createMynthImage({\n  apiKey: process.env.MYNTH_API_KEY!,\n  baseUrl: \"https://api.mynth.io\",\n});\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: mynth(\"google/gemini-3.1-flash-image\"),\n  prompt: \"A playful paper-cut illustration of a city park in spring\",\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.images[0]?.url);\n```\n\nYou can still override shared config per adapter:\n\n```ts\nimport { createMynthImage } from \"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\";\n\nconst mynth = createMynthImage();\n\nconst adapter = mynth(\"auto\", {\n  baseUrl: \"https://proxy.example.com\",\n});\n```\n\n## Model Options\n\nUse TanStack's top-level fields for common options such as `prompt`, `numberOfImages`, and shorthand `size`. Use `modelOptions` for Mynth-specific options:\n\n```ts\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { mynthImage } from \"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: mynthImage(\"recraft/recraft-v4\"),\n  prompt: \"Modern poster design for a jazz festival\",\n  numberOfImages: 2,\n  size: \"portrait\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    negativePrompt: \"watermark, blurry text\",\n    magicPrompt: true,\n    size: {\n      type: \"aspect_ratio\",\n      aspectRatio: \"4:5\",\n      scale: \"4k\",\n    },\n    output: {\n      format: \"png\",\n      quality: 90,\n    },\n    rating: true,\n    metadata: {\n      requestId: \"req_123\",\n    },\n  },\n});\n```\n\nNotes:\n\n- `modelOptions.negativePrompt` maps to Mynth's `negative_prompt`, and `modelOptions.magicPrompt` maps to `magic_prompt`\n- `modelOptions.rating` configures content rating on the result. The older `contentRating` name still works as an alias\n- `modelOptions.promptStructured` is still supported for compatibility and expands into `prompt`, `negative_prompt`, and `magic_prompt`. When set, its `positive` overrides the plain `prompt`\n- `modelOptions.size` overrides the top-level `size`. Use it when you need structured Mynth size objects, including aspect ratios and an optional `scale: \"4k\"`\n- Top-level `size` is for shorthand values such as `\"auto\"` and preset strings like `\"square\"` or `\"landscape\"`\n- `modelOptions.destination` delivers the generation to a configured Mynth destination, overriding any adapter-level or env default\n\n## Image Inputs (image-to-image)\n\nModels that accept image inputs work with TanStack AI's content-part prompts, so you can mix instruction text with reference images for image-to-image, reference-guided, edit, and try-on flows. The adapter maps the image parts onto Mynth's `inputs`:\n\n```ts\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { mynthImage } from \"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: mynthImage(\"black-forest-labs/flux.2-dev\"),\n  prompt: [\n    { type: \"text\", content: \"Restyle this scene as a watercolor painting\" },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/photo.jpg\" },\n    },\n  ],\n});\n```\n\nA few things worth knowing:\n\n- Only models in `MYNTH_IMAGE_INPUT_MODELS` accept image parts. Passing image parts to a text-only model is a compile-time error\n- Both URL sources (`{ type: \"url\", value }`) and inline data sources (`{ type: \"data\", value, mimeType }`, encoded as a data URI) are supported\n- A part's `metadata.role` maps to Mynth's input intent. TanStack's `\"character\"` maps directly, and the other generic roles fall back to Mynth's automatic detection\n- For Mynth's finer-grained intents (`person`, `garment`, `pose`, `style`, `background`, `product`, `object`), pass `modelOptions.inputs` with an explicit `as`\n- Image parts from the prompt and entries in `modelOptions.inputs` are combined, with prompt parts first\n\n## Available Models\n\nThe adapter exports a runtime list and a type union for supported image models:\n\n```ts\nimport { MYNTH_IMAGE_MODELS, type MynthImageModel } from \"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\";\n\nconst defaultModel: MynthImageModel = \"auto\";\n\nfor (const model of MYNTH_IMAGE_MODELS) {\n  console.log(model);\n}\n```\n\nThis is handy for model selectors, validation, and keeping client and server code in sync. There is a matching `MYNTH_IMAGE_INPUT_MODELS` list (and `MynthImageInputModel` type) for the subset that accepts image inputs.\n\nMynth supports model IDs across multiple providers, including `auto`, Flux, Recraft, Gemini, Qwen, Seedream, Imagine, Wan, Grok Imagine, and try-on models. The exported list is a fixed snapshot for type safety. For the live catalog with pricing, use the models endpoint below.\n\n### Models endpoint\n\nMynth exposes a public catalog at `https://api.mynth.io/models`. It does not require an API key, and it carries pricing today with room for more metadata over time. This is the source of truth if you want to render a picker with live pricing rather than the static exported list.\n\n```ts\nconst response = await fetch(\"https://api.mynth.io/models\");\nconst { data } = await response.json();\n\nfor (const model of data) {\n  console.log(model.id, model.displayName, model.pricing);\n}\n```\n\nEach entry looks roughly like this:\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"id\": \"black-forest-labs/flux.2-dev\",\n  \"displayName\": \"FLUX.2 Dev\",\n  \"pricing\": {\n    \"perImage\": { \"base\": \"0.01\", \"4k\": \"0.04\" },\n    \"perInput\": \"0.002\",\n  },\n}\n```\n\nIf you already use the Mynth SDK, the same data is available through `new Mynth().models.list()`.\n\n## Streaming Example\n\nThis adapter also works with TanStack AI's streaming image workflow:\n\n```ts\nimport { generateImage, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { mynthImage } from \"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { prompt, model } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = generateImage({\n    adapter: mynthImage(model ?? \"auto\"),\n    prompt,\n    numberOfImages: 1,\n    stream: true,\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\nFor a full example using `useGenerateImage()`, see the [TanStack Start + Mynth adapter demo](https://github.com/mynthio/oss/tree/main/examples/tanstack-start-ai-mynth-adapter).\n\n## Supported Capabilities\n\n- Image generation with `generateImage()`\n- Image-to-image with content-part prompts on input-capable models\n- Streaming image generation with `stream: true`\n- Typed model IDs through `MYNTH_IMAGE_MODELS` and `MynthImageModel`\n- Mynth-specific request options through `modelOptions`\n\nThe adapter returns TanStack AI's normalized image result shape:\n\n- `id`: the Mynth task id\n- `model`: the resolved model returned by Mynth, or the requested model as a fallback\n- `images`: only successful images are included\n- `images[*].revisedPrompt`: included when Mynth enhances the prompt\n\n## API Reference\n\n### `mynthImage(model, config?)`\n\nCreates a Mynth image adapter directly.\n\n- `model`: a `MynthImageModel`\n- `config.apiKey?`: optional override for `MYNTH_API_KEY`\n- `config.baseUrl?`: optional base URL override\n- `config.destination?`: optional default destination for generated images\n\nReturns a `MynthImageAdapter` for use with `generateImage()`.\n\n### `createMynthImage(config?)`\n\nCreates a reusable provider factory that returns model-bound adapters.\n\n### `MYNTH_IMAGE_MODELS`\n\nReadonly array of supported Mynth image model IDs.\n\n### `MynthImageModel`\n\nType union of supported Mynth image model IDs.\n\n### `MYNTH_IMAGE_INPUT_MODELS`\n\nReadonly array of model IDs that accept image inputs (image-to-image, try-on).\n\n### `MynthImageInputModel`\n\nType union of the model IDs that accept image inputs.\n\n## Limitations\n\n- This package only provides an image adapter for `generateImage()`\n- It does not provide chat or text-generation adapters\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Mynth SDK README](https://github.com/mynthio/oss/tree/main/packages/sdk)\n- [TanStack Start + Mynth adapter demo](https://github.com/mynthio/oss/tree/main/examples/tanstack-start-ai-mynth-adapter)\n- [Mynth](https://mynth.io)\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Mynth\nid: mynth-adapter\ndescription: \"Generate images with Mynth models like Flux, Recraft, Gemini, Qwen, Seedream, Wan, and Grok Imagine in TanStack AI via the Mynth community adapter.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - mynth\n  - image generation\n  - flux\n  - recraft\n  - qwen\n  - seedream\n  - community adapter\n---\n\nThe Mynth adapter gives you access to Mynth image generation models through TanStack AI. It is a community adapter for `generateImage()` with typed model IDs, normalized image results, image-to-image support, and Mynth-specific request options through `modelOptions`.\n\nMynth is image-only in this package. Reach for it when you want TanStack AI's image generation workflow with Mynth models such as Flux, Recraft, Gemini, Qwen, Seedream, Wan, and Grok Imagine.\n\nQuick note: Mynth is in public beta, so the model lineup and a few request options are still settling. The adapter tracks the Mynth SDK closely, and we welcome feedback on the API and integration experience.\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter @tanstack/ai\nvue: @mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter @tanstack/ai\nsolid: @mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter @tanstack/ai\nsvelte: @mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter @tanstack/ai\npreact: @mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter @tanstack/ai\nangular: @mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter @tanstack/ai\nvanilla: @mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter @tanstack/ai\noctane: @mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter @tanstack/ai\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nThe adapter targets `@tanstack/ai` 0.34 and newer.\n\n## Authentication\n\nSet your Mynth API key in the environment:\n\n```sh\nMYNTH_API_KEY=mak_...\n```\n\nKeep `MYNTH_API_KEY` on the server only. Never expose it in browser code or public client environment variables, or it may end up in a client bundle.\n\nYou can also pass `apiKey` directly in the adapter config. `baseUrl` is optional and useful for proxies, tests, or custom deployments.\n\nIf you need a key, create one in the [Mynth API keys dashboard](https://mynth.io/dashboard/keys).\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```ts\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { mynthImage } from \"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: mynthImage(\"black-forest-labs/flux.2-dev\"),\n  prompt: \"Editorial product photo of a ceramic mug on a linen tablecloth\",\n  numberOfImages: 1,\n  size: \"square\",\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.id);\nconsole.log(result.model);\nconsole.log(result.images[0]?.url);\n```\n\nTanStack AI adapters are model-bound, so you choose the Mynth model when you create the adapter.\n\n## Reusable Provider\n\nUse `createMynthImage()` when you want to share config across multiple adapters:\n\n```ts\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { createMynthImage } from \"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\";\n\nconst mynth = createMynthImage({\n  apiKey: process.env.MYNTH_API_KEY!,\n  baseUrl: \"https://api.mynth.io\",\n});\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: mynth(\"google/gemini-3.1-flash-image\"),\n  prompt: \"A playful paper-cut illustration of a city park in spring\",\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.images[0]?.url);\n```\n\nYou can still override shared config per adapter:\n\n```ts\nimport { createMynthImage } from \"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\";\n\nconst mynth = createMynthImage();\n\nconst adapter = mynth(\"auto\", {\n  baseUrl: \"https://proxy.example.com\",\n});\n```\n\n## Model Options\n\nUse TanStack's top-level fields for common options such as `prompt`, `numberOfImages`, and shorthand `size`. Use `modelOptions` for Mynth-specific options:\n\n```ts\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { mynthImage } from \"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: mynthImage(\"recraft/recraft-v4\"),\n  prompt: \"Modern poster design for a jazz festival\",\n  numberOfImages: 2,\n  size: \"portrait\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    negativePrompt: \"watermark, blurry text\",\n    magicPrompt: true,\n    size: {\n      type: \"aspect_ratio\",\n      aspectRatio: \"4:5\",\n      scale: \"4k\",\n    },\n    output: {\n      format: \"png\",\n      quality: 90,\n    },\n    rating: true,\n    metadata: {\n      requestId: \"req_123\",\n    },\n  },\n});\n```\n\nNotes:\n\n- `modelOptions.negativePrompt` maps to Mynth's `negative_prompt`, and `modelOptions.magicPrompt` maps to `magic_prompt`\n- `modelOptions.rating` configures content rating on the result. The older `contentRating` name still works as an alias\n- `modelOptions.promptStructured` is still supported for compatibility and expands into `prompt`, `negative_prompt`, and `magic_prompt`. When set, its `positive` overrides the plain `prompt`\n- `modelOptions.size` overrides the top-level `size`. Use it when you need structured Mynth size objects, including aspect ratios and an optional `scale: \"4k\"`\n- Top-level `size` is for shorthand values such as `\"auto\"` and preset strings like `\"square\"` or `\"landscape\"`\n- `modelOptions.destination` delivers the generation to a configured Mynth destination, overriding any adapter-level or env default\n\n## Image Inputs (image-to-image)\n\nModels that accept image inputs work with TanStack AI's content-part prompts, so you can mix instruction text with reference images for image-to-image, reference-guided, edit, and try-on flows. The adapter maps the image parts onto Mynth's `inputs`:\n\n```ts\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { mynthImage } from \"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: mynthImage(\"black-forest-labs/flux.2-dev\"),\n  prompt: [\n    { type: \"text\", content: \"Restyle this scene as a watercolor painting\" },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/photo.jpg\" },\n    },\n  ],\n});\n```\n\nA few things worth knowing:\n\n- Only models in `MYNTH_IMAGE_INPUT_MODELS` accept image parts. Passing image parts to a text-only model is a compile-time error\n- Both URL sources (`{ type: \"url\", value }`) and inline data sources (`{ type: \"data\", value, mimeType }`, encoded as a data URI) are supported\n- A part's `metadata.role` maps to Mynth's input intent. TanStack's `\"character\"` maps directly, and the other generic roles fall back to Mynth's automatic detection\n- For Mynth's finer-grained intents (`person`, `garment`, `pose`, `style`, `background`, `product`, `object`), pass `modelOptions.inputs` with an explicit `as`\n- Image parts from the prompt and entries in `modelOptions.inputs` are combined, with prompt parts first\n\n## Available Models\n\nThe adapter exports a runtime list and a type union for supported image models:\n\n```ts\nimport { MYNTH_IMAGE_MODELS, type MynthImageModel } from \"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\";\n\nconst defaultModel: MynthImageModel = \"auto\";\n\nfor (const model of MYNTH_IMAGE_MODELS) {\n  console.log(model);\n}\n```\n\nThis is handy for model selectors, validation, and keeping client and server code in sync. There is a matching `MYNTH_IMAGE_INPUT_MODELS` list (and `MynthImageInputModel` type) for the subset that accepts image inputs.\n\nMynth supports model IDs across multiple providers, including `auto`, Flux, Recraft, Gemini, Qwen, Seedream, Imagine, Wan, Grok Imagine, and try-on models. The exported list is a fixed snapshot for type safety. For the live catalog with pricing, use the models endpoint below.\n\n### Models endpoint\n\nMynth exposes a public catalog at `https://api.mynth.io/models`. It does not require an API key, and it carries pricing today with room for more metadata over time. This is the source of truth if you want to render a picker with live pricing rather than the static exported list.\n\n```ts\nconst response = await fetch(\"https://api.mynth.io/models\");\nconst { data } = await response.json();\n\nfor (const model of data) {\n  console.log(model.id, model.displayName, model.pricing);\n}\n```\n\nEach entry looks roughly like this:\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"id\": \"black-forest-labs/flux.2-dev\",\n  \"displayName\": \"FLUX.2 Dev\",\n  \"pricing\": {\n    \"perImage\": { \"base\": \"0.01\", \"4k\": \"0.04\" },\n    \"perInput\": \"0.002\",\n  },\n}\n```\n\nIf you already use the Mynth SDK, the same data is available through `new Mynth().models.list()`.\n\n## Streaming Example\n\nThis adapter also works with TanStack AI's streaming image workflow:\n\n```ts\nimport { generateImage, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { mynthImage } from \"@mynthio/tanstack-ai-adapter\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { prompt, model } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = generateImage({\n    adapter: mynthImage(model ?? \"auto\"),\n    prompt,\n    numberOfImages: 1,\n    stream: true,\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\nFor a full example using `useGenerateImage()`, see the [TanStack Start + Mynth adapter demo](https://github.com/mynthio/oss/tree/main/examples/tanstack-start-ai-mynth-adapter).\n\n## Supported Capabilities\n\n- Image generation with `generateImage()`\n- Image-to-image with content-part prompts on input-capable models\n- Streaming image generation with `stream: true`\n- Typed model IDs through `MYNTH_IMAGE_MODELS` and `MynthImageModel`\n- Mynth-specific request options through `modelOptions`\n\nThe adapter returns TanStack AI's normalized image result shape:\n\n- `id`: the Mynth task id\n- `model`: the resolved model returned by Mynth, or the requested model as a fallback\n- `images`: only successful images are included\n- `images[*].revisedPrompt`: included when Mynth enhances the prompt\n\n## API Reference\n\n### `mynthImage(model, config?)`\n\nCreates a Mynth image adapter directly.\n\n- `model`: a `MynthImageModel`\n- `config.apiKey?`: optional override for `MYNTH_API_KEY`\n- `config.baseUrl?`: optional base URL override\n- `config.destination?`: optional default destination for generated images\n\nReturns a `MynthImageAdapter` for use with `generateImage()`.\n\n### `createMynthImage(config?)`\n\nCreates a reusable provider factory that returns model-bound adapters.\n\n### `MYNTH_IMAGE_MODELS`\n\nReadonly array of supported Mynth image model IDs.\n\n### `MynthImageModel`\n\nType union of supported Mynth image model IDs.\n\n### `MYNTH_IMAGE_INPUT_MODELS`\n\nReadonly array of model IDs that accept image inputs (image-to-image, try-on).\n\n### `MynthImageInputModel`\n\nType union of the model IDs that accept image inputs.\n\n## Limitations\n\n- This package only provides an image adapter for `generateImage()`\n- It does not provide chat or text-generation adapters\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Mynth SDK README](https://github.com/mynthio/oss/tree/main/packages/sdk)\n- [TanStack Start + Mynth adapter demo](https://github.com/mynthio/oss/tree/main/examples/tanstack-start-ai-mynth-adapter)\n- [Mynth](https://mynth.io)\n"}
